            <h2>Circuit Diagrams — Interview-Ready Schematics</h2>

            <h3>Voltage Divider</h3>
            <div class="circuit-diagram">
Vin ─────────[R1]─────┬─── Vout<br>
                      │<br>
                     [R2]<br>
                      │<br>
                     GND<br><br>
Vout = Vin · R2/(R1+R2)
            </div>
            <p><strong>The single most-asked circuit at any Tier-1 core interview.</strong></p>

            <h3>RC Low-Pass Filter</h3>
            <div class="circuit-diagram">
Vin ─────────[R]─────┬─── Vout<br>
                     │<br>
                    [C]<br>
                     │<br>
                    GND<br><br>
ωc = 1/RC (corner frequency)<br>
Slope: −20 dB/decade beyond ωc
            </div>

            <h3>Inverting Op-Amp Amplifier</h3>
            <div class="circuit-diagram">
         ┌─────[Rf]────┐<br>
         │             │<br>
Vin ─[Rin]─→(−)       │<br>
         │             ├──┬─── Vout<br>
         └─(+) OpAmp   │<br>
              │        │<br>
             GND      GND<br><br>
Vout = −(Rf/Rin) · Vin
            </div>

            <h3>NPN BJT as a Switch</h3>
            <div class="circuit-diagram">
        +Vcc<br>
         │<br>
        [Rc]<br>
         │<br>
        LED<br>
         │<br>
        ─┤C (BJT)<br>
        ─┤B<br>
        ─┤E<br>
         │<br>
        [Rb]<br>
         │<br>
Vin ─────┴──── GND<br><br>
Vin > 0.7 V drives base current, transistor saturates, LED glows.
            </div>

            <h3>555 Timer in Astable Mode</h3>
            <div class="circuit-diagram">
       +Vcc<br>
         │<br>
        [Ra]<br>
         │<br>
        ┌┴─────[Rb]─────┐<br>
        │                │<br>
       [C]              OUT<br>
        │<br>
       GND<br><br>
Frequency ≈ 1.44 / ((Ra+2Rb)·C)<br>
Duty cycle = (Ra+Rb)/(Ra+2Rb)
            </div>

            <h3>Arduino UNO — LED + Resistor</h3>
            <div class="circuit-diagram">
Arduino D13 ─────[220Ω]─→[LED]→ GND<br><br>
digitalWrite(13, HIGH) blinks the LED.
            </div>
